{
  "about": "Dates and times on the clock a series repeats on (cal_core::wall_clock, DESIGN-series-time-zone.md stage 8, decision 100a). Each question is answered with the clock read (the canonical zone, null for UTC) and: wallOf the date, HH:MM time and seconds an instant shows; instantOf how a typed wall time reads (single, fold with the earlier instant and the later one, gap with the offsets before and after, in seconds east of UTC); untilOn the day's last second on the clock: 23:59:59, or the second before the change where one skips the day's end (Nuuk), absent only where the clock skips the whole day (Apia). seriesEnd how a stored UNTIL reads on the clock the series repeats on (its zone, UTC, or for an all-day series the device's): throughDay, instant or wall, the bound as a wall time, the last instant at or before it, and the last day it reaches; …T235959Z on a zone's clock is through that day unless the second after it is one of the rule's times of day, as after a cut (decisions 101b, 105a-116a). null for text that names no instant, date or time. Written by hand from tzdata's rules (Berlin, New York, Lord Howe, Apia 2011, Paris LMT +00:09:21) and checked against Node's ICU zone data; the core and both surfaces read this file.",
